---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';

const path = '/use-cases/welcome-series';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/welcome-series');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/welcome-series');
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Build a Shopify welcome series around the signup promise</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">Help a new subscriber understand the store and take an appropriate first step, while keeping a returning customer out of a first-order pitch.</p>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-12 max-w-4xl p-8">
      <h2>Start with what the subscriber requested</h2>
      <p>Record the signup source, channel permission and the specific promise shown on the form. A requested size guide, launch update and discount code need different opening messages. Deliver the promised resource before adding a store introduction. A checkout contact is not automatically a new marketing subscriber; have the operator establish channel eligibility.</p>
      <h2>Resolve customer identity before an offer</h2>
      <p>Check whether the address belongs to an existing customer or merges with a profile that has purchased. Re-subscribing should not silently renew a first-order benefit. Keep the resource useful for returning customers while changing the purchase invitation. Define how guest checkout orders and delayed order imports update the queued journey.</p>
      <h2>Sequence help rather than a fixed clock</h2>
      <p>Use the first message to fulfill the promise, then address a relevant purchase barrier such as fit, compatibility or delivery coverage. Choose spacing from the promise and observed response rather than copying a universal schedule. A cart journey may take priority; a purchase should end the acquisition pitch and hand off to post-purchase help.</p>
      <h2>Select tools for capture-to-message continuity</h2>
      <p>Ask candidates to demonstrate how form source and permission reach the first message, how an issued code is retrieved after a retry, and how duplicate signups are handled. If Sequenzy is on the shortlist, require this same demonstration before assigning it the workflow. Compare setup and support effort alongside message costs; do not infer capability from a ranking.</p>
      <h2>Proposed signup rehearsal and evaluation</h2>
      <p>Use staff profiles for a new subscriber, returning buyer, repeated form submission and purchase while a message is queued. Check resource delivery, duplicate prevention, offer eligibility and the exit to customer education. These are proposed checks, not completed tests. Evaluate first purchases and contribution across eligible signups, accounting for discounts, returns and channel costs; opens alone do not establish acquisition value.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
